WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:05.180
Obviously is quite a problem

00:00:05.529 --> 00:00:13.150
how do you make D2O, because normally
the deuterium in the water is diluted by

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:18.189
a factor of seven thousand. Which for
chemist is really pretty dilute.

00:00:18.189 --> 00:00:23.230
The best way of making D2O is by a process
called electrolysis when you pass a

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:30.009
current through the water to make
hydrogen. The process was first carried

00:00:30.009 --> 00:00:35.289
out on the large scale in Norway just
before the second world war.

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:41.280
In Norway which is a very mountainous country they
have a lot of cheap electricity from

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:43.450
hydropower.

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:49.360
Rivers going over waterfalls. So they
have electricity and it makes economic

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:55.810
sense to generate hydrogen to make ...
for making ammonia and fertilizers by

00:00:55.810 --> 00:01:03.190
electrolyzing water. And if you
electrolyze water you find that the H2O

00:01:03.190 --> 00:01:11.829
react a little bit faster than the D2O.
So if you go on electrolyzing more and

00:01:11.829 --> 00:01:17.020
more of water and keeping what's left
and then doing several stages of

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:22.899
electrolysis you can gradually
concentrate more and more of the D2O

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:30.240
To eventually it's nearly pure. This process was
carried out in a fairly remote power

00:01:30.249 --> 00:01:38.139
station in central Norway. In a region called Telemark. Now, one of the main uses of

00:01:38.139 --> 00:01:46.060
D2O in the early stages of nuclear
science was for making nuclear reactors.

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:51.969
Nuclear piles, and during the Second
World War the British and the Americans

00:01:51.969 --> 00:01:59.170
were terrified that Germany who occupied
Norway in ... that time might get

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:05.619
hold of the D2O and start nuclear
research. And in one of the best raids of

00:02:05.619 --> 00:02:09.270
the whole Second World War six
Norwegians

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:18.060
attacked the power station, destroyed the
heavy-water apparatus and retreated.

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:22.770
And the reason it was so successful is that
nobody was injured and nobody was killed.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:28.800
So they got into the place blew it up
and escaped without anybody being

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:34.560
injured and in fact the German General
that investigated thought it was one of

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:36.540
them as magnificent military feats

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:42.240
he'd ever seen. There's another story
that before the Germans invaded Norway,

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:49.680
that the supply of heavy water - two cans - a few gallons, was smuggled out to the UK.

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:57.180
And it was so valuable it is said that
it was put under King George VI bed

00:02:57.180 --> 00:03:03.360
overnight so it should be safe before it
was then transported to America.

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:04.220
Is that true?

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:09.060
Well this is the the legend and the
story is that when it was flown to

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:11.970
America in an unheated plane

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:16.320
the water froze, so when the people took
it off

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:21.330
it sounded as if the cans were empty and
they got really worried but then it

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:24.330
warmed up and melted.

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:33.070
D2O has a number of applications but
it's real use is in a technique called

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:35.020
nuclear magnetic resonance.

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:39.760
We have shown it on our video about tea,
how you can use it to analyze molecules.

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:45.600
And nuclear magnetic resonance is very
sensitive to hydrogen atoms.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:49.660
So if you want to study some sort of molecules
dissolved in water

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:55.240
if you use ordinary water, the hydrogen
atoms in the water have such a strong

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:59.290
signal, that you can't study the
dissolved molecules at all.

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:06.400
So instead you use D2O which do not
respond to the same frequencies as the

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:08.770
hydrogen and so you get a nice spectrum.

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:11.770
[Brady] I think people watching will have two
questions.

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:17.320
What does heavy water tastes like? And
what will happen to me if I think it?

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:20.500
Well, I've never tasted D2O.

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:27.610
I suspect that it will taste really
quite similar to H2O. Though it's

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:32.500
difficult to predict because sometimes
things taste quite different, but water

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:34.210
doesn't really taste anyway,

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:39.850
you usually tastes what's dissolved in
the water salts or whatever.

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:46.480
There is a strong body of opinion that D2O is
quite poisonous and the reason why it's

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:53.830
poisonous is because in your body you
have all sorts of molecules that have

00:04:53.830 --> 00:05:00.700
hydrogen bonded particularly to oxygen. And these bonds break as part of the

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:03.310
various chemical processes in your body.

00:05:03.310 --> 00:05:10.510
Deuterium oxygen bonds are slightly
stronger than hydrogen oxygen bonds and

00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:16.120
therefore if you start changing your
body for the the chemicals in your body

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:22.810
from hydrogen to deuterium these bonds 
will break more slowly. And so various

00:05:22.810 --> 00:05:26.950
processes in your body are likely to
slow right down.

00:05:27.490 --> 00:05:30.550
If they slow down they may completely
stop.

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:35.200
Well I was always told that you could
kill someone by making a cup of tea

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:35.890
with D2O.

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:37.330
Because what it does

00:05:37.330 --> 00:05:41.900
is there a difference between the way
that hydrogen reacts and deuterium reacts

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:45.100
in the body so it can replace hydrogen
in the body and obviously its everywhere

00:05:45.100 --> 00:05:47.860
it's in the water and it's in all the enzymes 
that are in your body.

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:52.599
But I have since read that
apparently you need to replace about fifty

00:05:52.599 --> 00:05:56.139
percent of the water in your body. For
actually kill you with D2O, which is

00:05:56.139 --> 00:05:57.939
kind of impractical.

00:05:57.939 --> 00:06:01.099
So ... would be murderers don't try that one, it will not work.

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:08.500
There is a rumor which I never been able to verify that the Argonne lab in the United States just outside

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:15.620
Chicago at one time had deuterated a
dog, which had been brought up and fed on D2O.

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:20.979
But I think this is probably just a
urban myth, and it never happened.

00:06:20.979 --> 00:06:28.479
There's also a suggestion that if you
dilute your whiskey with D2O rather

00:06:28.479 --> 00:06:33.370
than H2O, that you might not get so dizzy
when you drink too much.

00:06:33.969 --> 00:06:40.389
But you might be dead so it's not
something that one should try and anyway

00:06:40.389 --> 00:06:42.049
it's far too expensive.

